      "writtenOn": "2022-01-22T00:26:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So naming is hard. We have inconsistency between our legacy upper caase naming and the final Zephyr naming (which presumably will be lower case).\nMost internal DTS references seem to be lower case.\n\nThe good thing is that the labels are completely up to the implementor, who can use upper or lower case as they want - though in DTS we may want to keep\nthem lower case.\n\nWithin our code, we can suggest to always use GPIO_DT_LABEL, which does resolve down to the DT_GPIO_\u003cenum\u003e anyway. Consistency is good here, and the less use we make of the enum-name, the better.",
      "parentUuid": "024685db_f7ab65d0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 30,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 30,
        "endChar": 53
